<p>Pope Leo XIV began a 10-day trip to Africa on Monday with the first-ever papal visit to Algeria, before continuing to Cameroon, Angola and Equatorial Guinea in the most ambitious journey of his pontificate so far. Across the four-country tour, Leo is expected to emphasize peace, inequality and interfaith dialogue while spotlighting the needs of Catholic communities across the continent.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wJmjWfyTxhK7XWxWnSLJ2XjyeTrmiMFtAZLy2eIvuqhq5dsfxNrRoz6vaMbe6F38E0ZIcfpko-1fHOnIbqiTS7KXYCk8vwiB5c6jaF8ApTCRfaEDkNLQ5ypu4-dykel2JjAxL6XlSnA5lQhKuN0hj2F06xeI8UuFtFHb9k1RoKlbOlpPFeI5-A4SGsDmCa1hWGMC2tMIrVDRdFIBG1DjxqjG94HDe3iYmJcKR8YH' alt='Pope Leo XIV at the Vatican last month. His 10-day trip to Africa begins on Monday and includes visits to Algeria, Angola, Cameroon and Equatorial Guinea.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Heavy itinerary: The trip spans 11 cities and towns, nearly 18,000 km and 18 flights, illustrating the scale of the Vatican’s effort to engage the continent directly.</li><li>Two-day Algeria stay: Leo is scheduled to spend two days in Algeria before moving on, giving added weight to the first-ever papal stop there.</li><li>Vulnerable communities: The New York Times says the voyage reflects Leo’s urgent focus on some of the Church’s most vulnerable members on the world’s poorest continent.</li><li>First U.S. pope: The four-country swing highlights Leo’s place as the first U.S. pope.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Vatican aides: They describe the trip as an effort to place the world’s attention on Africa and on vulnerable Catholic communities whose needs Leo wants to emphasize. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0jyx4qq7o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: The Algeria leg is presented as both a return to the country’s deep Christian past through St. Augustine and a gesture of outreach to Muslims in a nation where Christians are a tiny minority. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/le-monde-africa/article/2026/04/13/in-algeria-the-pope-follows-in-the-footsteps-of-the-country-s-christian-history-and-reaches-out-to-muslims_6752354_124.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The paper frames the journey as a meeting with the future of Catholicism, while noting Leo will also have to navigate visits with authoritarian leaders. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/13/world/europe/pope-leo-africa-future.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/pope-making-papal-visit-algeria-launch-africa-trip-131983253'>Pope making first papal visit to Algeria to launch Africa trip, honor St. Augustine</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/le-monde-africa/article/2026/04/13/in-algeria-the-pope-follows-in-the-footsteps-of-the-country-s-christian-history-and-reaches-out-to-muslims_6752354_124.html'>In Algeria, the pope follows in the footsteps of the country&#x27;s Christian history and reaches out to Muslims</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604130099.html'>Africa: Pope Leo Sets Off on African Tour Focused on Peace and Unity</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/pope-leo-to-begin-10-day-africa-tour-on-mission-to-spotlight-continents-needs'>Pope Leo to begin 10-day Africa tour on mission to spotlight continent’s needs</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0jyx4qq7o'>Pope prioritises world&#x27;s fastest-growing Catholic region in major Africa tour</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/13/world/europe/what-to-know-pope-africa.html'>What to Know About Pope Leo’s Voyage to Africa</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/pope-leo-10-day-africa-tour-continents-needs/article70856078.ece'>Pope Leo to begin 10-day Africa tour on mission to spotlight continent&#x27;s needs</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>